Subject: [PATCH] nebula: Layer A @NebulaRW annotations on entity hot path
 (D15)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Annotates 6 entity hot-path methods per architecture §14.3 Phase 1
Month 4-6 (the ~50 entity functions called for):

Entity:
  - tick() — self-write, position read, ENTITY_MOVED event
  - move(MoverType, Vec3) — collision-zone block read, position/velocity/onGround write
  - rideTick() — self + vehicle read, position/velocity write

LivingEntity:
  - tick() — full self read/write (covers hurt/death state)
  - aiStep() — physics step, position/deltaMovement/fallDistance write

Mob:
  - tick() — sensor scan over * entities (read-only), self write
  - aiStep() — navigation/lookControl/movementControl, self position+rotation write

Each annotation declares maxRandomCalls (input to RandomBudget allocator)
and randomInstance (which RNG path is consumed). Conservative *-wildcard
reads are used where the actual closure is too dynamic to enumerate
statically (sensor scans, collision zones); RW-Guard runtime validation
(D17) will refine these once it observes actual accesses.

